<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert Bond</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1857">1857</a>–<a href="/years/1927">1927</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Robert Bond was Prime Minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a> from 1900 to 1909. He negotiated a reciprocity treaty with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in 1902, which the US Senate blocked, and pressed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> over French and American fishing rights on the island's coasts. Under him Newfoundland was granted the status of a dominion at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperial-conference">Imperial Conference</a> of 1907.</p></div>
